  "introduction": {
    "title": "What is a Microphone Preamp?",
    "text": "A microphone preamp (pre-amplifier) boosts the very weak signal from microphones to line level, making it strong enough for further processing and recording. The preamp is often the most crucial component affecting the character and quality of your recordings.",
    "columns": [
      {
        "title": "Primary Functions",
        "text": "Amplification: Boost mic signal 40-60dB. Impedance Matching: Optimize signal transfer. Phantom Power: Supply +48V for condensers. Gain Control: Adjust input sensitivity. Signal Conditioning: Shape tone and character. Noise Control: Maintain high signal-to-noise ratio."
      },
      {
        "title": "Why Quality Matters",
        "text": "First component in recording chain. Sets noise floor for entire recording. Adds distinctive tonal character. Affects dynamic response and transients. Influences harmonic content. Cannot be \"fixed\" later in mix."
      }
    ]
  },
